HTML DOM

.used to access HTML elements 
    .most commonly using the element's id

API method - action done to an HTML element
API property - value that can be accessed on an HTML element 

>> using example:
    getElementById - document method
    myPara = getElementByID - retrieves the 'demo' element
    innerHTML - element property
    myPara.HTML - changes the property 


HTML DOM API Abilities
.finding and selecting elements
.changing element content and attributes
.adding, removing, or modifying elements
.changing CSS styles
.adding event listeners to react to user input  

DOM API is the standard for how to get, change, add, or delete HTML DOM elements
JS is the language used in browsers to access DOM through the API
